  "id": "osf-pinned-toolchain-and-assert-style",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-06T13:43:58.617Z",
  "title": "Pin Rust 1.99.0 in CI and normalise empty-collection assertions",
  "summary": "Two unrelated but small changes travel together. CI now installs and selects a pinned Rust 1.99.0 toolchain (with clippy and rustfmt) in both the build and lint jobs, because the dev container image still ships an older Rust. Across the osf crates, `assert!(x.is_empty())` is rewritten as `assert_eq!(x, Vec::<T>::new())` in unit and integration tests, so a failure prints the offending contents instead of a bare boolean. No production logic changes: the lint rules, config loader, reviewer roster, work-item reference scanner and moon report parser behave exactly as before.",
